<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/1st-century-bce">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sulla's civil war</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">83–82 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a> · Also known as Sulla's second civil war</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sulla">Sulla</a>'s civil war was fought in 83–82 BCE between Lucius Cornelius Sulla, returning from the war against Mithridates, and the Marian faction governing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>. Sulla landed at Brundisium, and with commanders such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pompey">Pompey</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marcus-licinius-crassus">Crassus</a> defeated the Marian and Samnite armies, finally at the Colline Gate outside Rome in November 82 BCE. He then became dictator and carried out bloody proscriptions.</p></div>
